.Dd May 29, 2026
.Dt CONVERT-TO-MD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm convert-to-md
.Nd convert simple text-like documents to Markdown
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Ar file ...
.Nm
.Fl t Ar type
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl o Ar output.md
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a pure Bash converter for creating Markdown from plain text, simple HTML,
and simple reStructuredText files.
.Pp
When file paths are provided,
.Nm
creates a Markdown file next to each source file by replacing the source
extension with
.Pa .md .
For example,
.Pa page.html
is written as
.Pa page.md .
.Pp
When input is piped on standard input,
.Nm
requires an explicit input type with
.Fl t
or
.Fl -type .
Piped output is written to standard output unless
.Fl o
is provided.
.Pp
This program intentionally does not use external document converters.
Because it is pure Bash, formats that require binary, archive, or layout
parsing are rejected instead of being converted incorrectly.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Overwrite an existing Markdown output file.
.Pp
Without this option,
.Nm
refuses to replace an existing output file.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage information and exit.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -output Ar file
Write piped conversion output to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.Pp
This option is only valid for piped input.
.It Fl t Ar type , Fl -type Ar type , Fl -format Ar type
Specify the input type for piped content.
.Pp
Supported values are
.Cm txt ,
.Cm html ,
.Cm htm ,
and
.Cm rst .
.El
.Sh SUPPORTED FORMATS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm txt
Copies plain text content directly into Markdown output.
.It Cm html , Cm htm
Performs simple HTML-to-Markdown conversion.
.Pp
Recognized HTML includes headings
.Aq h1
through
.Aq h6 ,
paragraphs, line breaks, unordered and ordered list containers, list items,
bold tags, italic tags, and simple links.
.It Cm rst
Performs simple reStructuredText-to-Markdown conversion.
.Pp
Recognized RST includes underline-style headings using repeated marker lines.
Basic inline markup such as bold and italic is generally left as-is because it
already resembles Markdown.
.El
.Sh UNSUPPORTED FORMATS
.Nm
rejects the following formats in pure Bash mode:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
RTF
.It
DOCX
.It
EPUB
.It
PDF
.El
.Pp
These formats require parsing binary data, archives, XML packages, or page
layout structures.
Use a dedicated converter such as Pandoc if those formats need full Markdown
conversion.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
The command exits with a non-zero status if any input file cannot be converted,
if an output file already exists without
.Fl f ,
if a required option value is missing, or if the input format is unsupported.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert local files and write Markdown files next to them:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./convert-to-md.sh notes.txt page.html doc.rst
.Ed
.Pp
Overwrite existing Markdown outputs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./convert-to-md.sh -f page.html
.Ed
.Pp
Convert HTML downloaded from the web and write to standard output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curl -L "https://example.com/page.html" | \&./convert-to-md.sh --type html
.Ed
.Pp
Convert HTML downloaded from the web and save it to a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curl -L "https://example.com/page.html" | \&./convert-to-md.sh --type html -o page.md
.Ed
.Pp
Force overwrite for piped output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curl -L "https://example.com/page.html" | \&./convert-to-md.sh --type html -f -o page.md
.Ed
.Sh LIMITATIONS
.Nm
is intentionally conservative.
It handles simple text-like markup but is not a complete HTML or RST parser.
Complex nested HTML, scripts, styles, tables, attributes beyond simple links,
and advanced RST directives may not convert correctly.
.Pp
For complete document conversion, use a real document parser or converter.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bash 1 ,
.Xr curl 1
